  "description": "This course provides students with a fundamental understanding of measurement and control engineering. It covers the principles, performance characteristics, and elements of measurement systems, including sensors, transducers, and signal processing. Students will learn to model and analyze system dynamics, transfer functions, and both time-domain and frequency-domain responses. The course also introduces basic control concepts such as feedback, stability, compensation, and PID control, enabling students to design and assess simple control systems. Through practical exercises and simulations, students will develop the skills to perform measurements, collect and interpret data, and evaluate the behavior of measurement and control systems.",
  "learning_outcomes": [
    {
      "No.": "1",
      "CLO Name": "CLO1",
      "CLO Details": "Explain the principles, structure, and performance characteristics of instrumentation and measurement systems."
    },
    {
      "No.": "2",
      "CLO Name": "CLO2",
      "CLO Details": "Identify, describe, and evaluate the operation of common sensors, transducers, and instrumentation elements used for measuring physical variables."
    },
    {
      "No.": "3",
      "CLO Name": "CLO3",
      "CLO Details": "Analyze system models, transfer functions, and both time-domain and frequency-domain responses of measurement and control systems."
    },
    {
      "No.": "4",
      "CLO Name": "CLO4",
      "CLO Details": "Apply fundamental control concepts—including feedback, stability criteria, compensation, and PID control—to design and assess basic control systems."
    },
    {
      "No.": "5",
      "CLO Name": "CLO5",
      "CLO Details": "Perform measurement procedures, collect and interpret data, and conduct laboratory experiments or simulations related to instrumentation and control."
    }
  ],
